# The client-CI regression list: one scenario per line, run by
# tools/client-ci-regress.sh. Format:
#
#   name[@label] [client-ci.sh flags] [-- eve-server flags]
#
# @label tells two runs of one scenario apart (log and result names). The
# runner adds --rootless, --gateway and the scenario's own timeout
# (EOCI_FCI_TIMEOUT_S), so only what a scenario NEEDS beyond that is here.
# @SCHOOL@ becomes the first school id in out/content/agents/schools.tsv.
#
# Flags a scenario needs, and why:
#   --dev            a dev world (client-ci.sh gives each one its own fresh world, for every
#                    --dev run, so no scenario inherits a pilot left in space)
#   --with-second    a second client (costs 2 of the runner's --jobs client budget); the
#                    server roster must be two deep, so
#                    `-- --character Alice --character Bob`
#   school=N         the character must start at a school station
#
#   --with-bots      an `eve-bots --control` link beside the server, for the GM's `/bots`
#                    (needs --dev: the server then runs in accounts mode, see client-ci.sh)
#
# The wing and fleet-mission scenarios have a bot half that needs that link;
# without --with-bots it records a SKIP and the server half still runs.
#
#   --serial         the runner's own flag (client-ci.sh never sees it): with --jobs N > 1
#                    this row waits until the parallel rows are done and then runs alone,
#                    in the owner's prefix, as every row did before --jobs. Marked:
#                    rows that assert a deadline of a few seconds or the world clock's
#                    exactness (warp, undock, park, destiny coalescing, a re-skin within
#                    3 s, a capsule gone within 5 s, a bubble or a disruptor's park within
#                    10 s), the rows that scale the world's clock (--time-scale,
#                    --training-scale), and every --with-bots row (a bot swarm's CPU is
#                    load the other slots' clocks feel). Lift a mark once clock.tsv shows
#                    the row green at the --jobs you run (docs/guides/client-ci.md).
#                    With --jobs 1 the mark does nothing and the order is the list's.

