# l6b-mining-events (#33): /motherlode begin announces to the pilot (OnServerMessage), status and end; needs eve-offline-server and a system with a belt
fci_motherlode
# fci-combat (#207): a second pilot tackled: scrambler (warp and MWD refused with the client's keys, status 104 up), point (warp refused, MWD runs), web (maxVelocity by the module's own factor), each released on deactivate; two clients
fci_tackle --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# fci-combat (#207): damp, painter and tracking disruptor move the target's own attribute sheet by the module's factor read from the client's dogma data and give it back; an ECM jams the target's lock (the `electronic` icon); two clients
fci_ewar --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# ewar-2bc (#106): tracking and guidance disruptors, remote sensor boosters and tracking computers on a second pilot's buff bar and attributes, and the ship and cargo scanner windows; unscripted modules; two clients
fci_ewar_2 --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# w21-neut-smart: a neutralizer drops a second pilot's capacitor by the module's own amount and a nosferatu moves its amount to the emptier source; the buff-bar slots ewEnergyNeut and ewEnergyVampire; two clients
fci_neut --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# w21-neut-smart: a smartbomb hurts a second pilot's ship and launched drones inside the field and neither outside it (park.GetDamageState); two clients
fci_smartbomb --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# abyss-0 (#91): /abyss enter 3 to an abyssal system (no celestials), one room and its exit gate, the abyss service's pushes, and AbyssalEndGateActivation home; the plain server
fci_abyss_enter
# abyss-1 (#92): a filament through the key window's call to three rooms (encounter gates, then the exit gate) and home; a refused co-op deploy; the plain server (needs a bundle with the abyssal filaments, rooms and typelists)
fci_abyss_run
# mjd-mass (#23): a battleship's Large Micro Jump Drive jumps ~100 km and keeps its speed; an MWD keeps the ego ball's mass equal to the ship item's; the plain server
fci_mjd
# bubbles-sb (#24): a sphere launcher in a null-sec system puts a probe ball in the park with warpDisruptionStartTime, a warp inside it raises WarpDisrupted, and the ball goes after its two minutes; the plain server (needs a bundle with the launcher and probe)
fci_bubble --serial
# nw-2 (#172): a Mobile Warp Disruptor is launched (free ball), anchored by the int-effect Activate (ball not free after anchoringDelay), refused a scoop, lifted and scooped; the plain server (needs a bundle regenerated with category 22)
fci_anchor_small
# nw-2 (#172): the same unit is no bubble while free or anchoring, raises WarpDisrupted once anchored with a force field at warpScrambleRange, and lets go on a lift; the plain server (needs the same bundle)
fci_mobile_bubble
# hic-script (#116): a Warp Disruption Field Generator runs with no script, and with a focused script loaded and no target the server refuses with DeniedActivateTargetNotPresent; the plain server (needs a bundle with the generator and script)
fci_hic_script --serial
# be-2 (#77): ship.Eject leaves the Merlin as an abandoned ball (not interactive, no charID), Board takes it back (capsule ball removed), a far Board is refused NotCloseEnoughToBoard, a dock puts the hull in the hangar; with a second client (#132) the lower-id pilot shoots the other's abandoned Merlin dead, its owner at a belt, and both combat logs list the mail; the plain server
fci_board_eject --with-second --serial -- --no-concord --character Alice --character Bob
# u4-upwell-dock (#64): /upwell spawn an Astrahus, Dock with the client's own route, the hangar lists the ship and answers as the structure, board a second hull and fit a module, Undock to space with the ego the ship, and once more; the plain server
fci_upwell_dock
# u6c (#115): take the controls of a structure (shipid becomes the structure, the tree gets the fuel and deed bays, an undock is refused), release them, and leave; the plain server
fci_upwell_control
# u4-upwell-dock (#64): Enter Structure (a live park whose ego is the structure), Undock from that view (no re-bind), then structure view -> hangar -> Undock (the re-bind inside the window); the plain server
fci_upwell_view
# u4-upwell-dock (#64): log off docked in a structure and select the character again (the docked login, the hangar, an Undock); the plain server. A server restart in between is the Rust test's
fci_upwell_relog
# u5-upwell-home (#65): in a spawned Astrahus the client's own repair service binds with the structure group, quotes the ship and RepairItems goes to RepairItemsInStructure; the plain server
fci_upwell_repair
# u5-upwell-home (#65): insurance through the structure bind (price, InsureShip, contract); the plain server
fci_upwell_insure
# u5-upwell-home (#65): InstallCloneInStation routed to InstallCloneInStructure, the clone listed at the structure, set_home_station(structure); the plain server
fci_upwell_clone
# u5-upwell-home (#65): home structure, /tr back to the start station, capsule, self_destruct_clone: wake in the structure with structureid keys and a new capsule; the plain server
fci_upwell_revive

# bp-3 (#120): a hostile hunter fitted with a smartbomb from its stock sets it off when two foes are in the field; one with a micro jump drive, tackled by a disruptor, jumps out (EVE_BOTS_KIT_DRILL grants the part in open mode, CI only)
fci_bot_smartbomb --with-bots --bots-kit smartbomb --serial -- --dev
fci_bot_mjd --with-bots --bots-kit mjd --serial -- --dev
# bp-4 (#121): a hostile hunter's web and scrambler are aimed by kind and reach (ewar_aim), not fired as guns; the client's buff bar shows webify and warpScramblerMWD (open-mode hunter setup grants the modules)
fci_bot_ewar_aim --with-bots --serial -- --dev
# fci-combat (#207): a hostile hunter-kind bot finds the client in a low-sec belt, locks it (GetTargetedBy) and hurts its ship (the client's own shield/armor/hull sheet)
fci_hunter_bot --with-bots --serial -- --dev
