# fci-travel (3.1): a real stargate jump out and back (warp to a gate of the park, menu.StargateJump, far-gate arrival, session/ship/park checks, CmdStop, jump back); the plain server
fci_gate_jump
# fci-travel (3.1): the client's own autopilot (SetWaypoint + autoPilot.SetOn) flies a 2-3 jump route, visiting each system in order and ending off at the destination; the plain server (needs the gates of the route loaded)
fci_autopilot
# fci-travel (3.1): a Black Ops hull jumps to a fleet mate's lit cyno in another null-sec system: refusal of a made-up beacon, session change, fuel spent, JumpActivation/JumpFatigue timers, landing near the field; two clients
fci_jump_drive --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# fci-travel (3.1): a Covert Jump Portal Generator opens a bridge to a fleet mate's cyno: the module alone does nothing, a made-up beacon is refused, both fleet services hold the bridge, fuel spent, ship held still, the portal closes by itself; no passenger step (needs a third pilot); two clients
fci_jump_portal --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord

# fci-services (master plan 3.1): the calendar: refusals (empty title, past, over 12 months, alliance with none), a personal event with an invitee and a corp event listed with owner and flag, details, responses both ways, a member refused edit, delete and corp events, edit and delete pushes; two clients
fci_calendar --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob

# fci-services (master plan 3.1): mail: refusals, send, push, sync, read/unread, reply bit, trash, restore, delete, and a mailing list (create, join, list mail both ways, mute refused, leave refused, delete); two clients
fci_mail --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob

# fci-services (master plan 3.1): player bounties: below-minimum, no-owner and over-wallet refusals, two contributions on a second pilot (wallet, pool, search, my-bounties, top page), the target's type-112 notifications; two clients; the kill payout is not here
fci_bounty --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob

# fci-services (master plan 3.1): a player war: refused declarations, a declare from the war HQ with its fee, both sides list it and hear OnWarChanged, spool-up then the GM's time help gives the can-fight flag on both clients, a surrender offer accepted with exact ISK, a forced peace; two clients
fci_war --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob

# fci-services (master plan 3.1): a reaction formula at an NPC station: listed as an original, the client's Job for activity 9 with its quote and no error codes, install (wallet, materials, a busy-formula refusal), the clock, delivery of an item stack in the quoted quantity, the formula kept; one client; fast job clock
fci_reactions --serial -- --time-scale 60
# w21-dd-inv: a GM titan fires the Lance at a second titan in null-sec: the empire refusal takes nothing, fuel and capacitor are paid, the immobility refuses A's warp and a second click, B sees OnSpecialFX effects.SWDamageBeam and takes damage; two clients
fci_doomsday --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# w21-dd-inv: a T1 blueprint copy is invented into a T2 blueprint with datacores: a copying job, an invention job, the delivery in the hangar and the industry window's blueprint list; time-scale 60 makes the jobs about two minutes
fci_invention --serial -- --time-scale 60
# w23-fit: the server refuses a module the hull cannot fit (wrong rack, no such slot, hull and size restriction, group limit, powergrid online refusal); the module stays in the hangar
fci_fit_refuse
# w23-fit: script-capable modules (sensor booster, tracking computer) run with no script, then take one
fci_script_empty
# w23-fit: an ECM burst breaks a second pilot's lock and the pilot can relock; two clients
fci_ecm_burst --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# w23-pve (#137): a Scorpion with a warp disruptor, a warp scrambler and a tracking disruptor on a belt rat: each runs and cycles, the rat stays on the grid, the pilot's own 104 is not moved, the rat stays no farther under the tracking disruptor; one client, needs belt rats
fci_rat_point
# w23-pve (#78): a pilot abandons a Merlin, another shoots it dead: one report for the hull on both sides (victim, final blow, ship types, system, the client's own drawing and hash lookup), the pod untouched; two clients
fci_abandon_kill --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob --no-concord
# w23-pve (#75): a fleet of one logs off and back on inside the two-minute window and is still in the fleet (session.fleetid, the fleet service, the server's composition); one client
fci_fleet_reconnect
